  parts: 100   score: 93/100
  critique: The ISO render reads instantly as an open-frame FPGA NTT card — eight glass BRAM banks down the back-left edge, the copper DSP-multiplier column, dark/steel symmetric add/sub pairs in an open rail-and-floor frame, the brass twiddle rail, the blue twiddle ROM, and the ten-fin exploded heatsink all nameable; FRONT/SIDE show nothing sunk below or floating off the ground line. Two real weaknesses persist. First, the headline exploded radix-4 butterfly still reads as a near-empty dark plate in SIDE view and its internal stage order (W1→W2→W3→j-rotator→add/sub→register) is legible only by reading roles, and nothing tells the viewer which of the four fused yokes it explodes. Second, the FPGA die is a featureless grey field in TOP, and crossbar_network still carried a buggy duplicate skewed bank map alongside the committed XOR-fold. The deeper residuals are all source-missing (paper's exact conflict-free map, σ_s, twiddle addressing) and belong to the evidence/amend loop, not geometry.
  + Purged the buggy duplicate skewed bank map bank(i)=(i+floor(i/8)) mod 8 from crossbar_network ops and notes, leaving only the committed GF(2)-linear XOR-fold map (matches addr_gen_unit / bram annotations); fixes the stride-512 collision the additive form caused.
  + Added two +X dataflow arrows (ex_flow_1 mult→add/sub, ex_flow_2 add/sub→register) on the exploded radix-4 unit so its left-to-right stage order is unambiguous without reading roles.
  + Added a thin carbon-fiber fusion-callout strut (lane_fusion_callout) tying the lanes-6/7 yoke up to the exploded baseplate, marking which fused unit the explode represents.
  + Scribed three thin raised die floorplan partitions (memory/array, array/reduction, control split) so the die reads as placed-and-routed zones in TOP without occluding mass.
  + Extended assembly_instructions steps 1 and 8 to cover the floorplan partitions, the exploded-unit dataflow arrows, and the fusion callout.
  · gap: SOURCE-MISSING (evidence/amend loop, not geometry): the paper's exact arbitrary-radix conflict-free (bank,offset) functions and per-stage crossbar permutation sigma_s (Sec. III headline) remain the committed XOR-fold stand-in; do not fabricate the paper's construction at the scene layer.
  · gap: SOURCE-MISSING: twiddle-ROM addressing f(stage,block) under the rearranged twiddle-reuse loop is still the committed CT/bit-reversed layout; the residual bit-reversed-vs-natural-order tension is noted in twiddle_rom spec and cannot be settled visually.
